Model Context Protocol:
It is used to connect AI agents with external tools and data through standardized protocol.
MCP Host – AI Application. It is responsible for running AI experience.
MCP Client – Component inside host that communicates with MCP server.
MCP Server – This is where capabilities are exposed.
Tool – Does something
Resource – Provide info/data.
MCP can also expose reusable prompt templates.
MCP Inspector – Testing tool for MCP server.

Practical Learning:
Created simple MCP Calculator and based on that I have created MCP server, tools and I have also run the MCP Inspector and also tested MCP tools.

References:
https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/getting-started/intro
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/artificial-intelligence/model-context-protocol-mcp/

03-09-2026
MCP Client - It connects AI application to MCP Server. It discovers available tools and call required tools.
LLM Integration - Integrated LLM with MCP to understand the user's request and select required MCP tools.

Practical Learning:
Created an MCP Client for the Calculator MCP Server and tested list of tools and call tools. Integrated Groq LLM with MCP. The LLM can select the required calculator tool based on the user's question, the MCP Client executes the tool, and the result is sent back to the LLM.

Flow:
User - Groq LLM - MCP Client - MCP Server - Tool - Result - LLM - Final Response.

04-09-2026
MCP Resources - Provide info or data to MCP Client. It is used to list and read available resources.
MCP Prompts - It is a reusable prompt template used to generate specific instructions for LLM
Database Integration - Connected a SQLite database with the MCP Server to store calculator expressions and results.

Practical Learning:
Created MCP Resources for calculator help and stored calculations. Created an MCP Prompt to explain calculations step by step. Connected a SQLite database and read the stored calculation data through an MCP resource

Flow:
MCP Client(Ask info) - MCP Server(Gives requested resource or prompt) - Resource/Prompt(Gives required info) - MCP Client(Receive info)